{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1547684-should-curse-dice-be-dice","id":1547684,"title":"Should curse dice be dice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-11T13:03:33-08:00","id":1547684,"title":"Should curse dice be dice?","content":"Curse dice don't really seem to do anything as actual dice. There's the altered outcomes, but they only happen when you cast a spell or if the storyteller feels like it, and they really shouldn't be happening very often. It seems like either curse dice should have a smaller more regular effect on the game, like hunger dice, or they should just be a pool of points to gain and spend, like vitae/essence/etc. Make it so you need a lot of curse dice to use your spells, but it's dangerous to have that much curse energy stored in your character all at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-16T05:30:13-08:00","id":1547776,"title":"","content":"FWIW in the Ashcan they were much more like Hunger Dice and it honestly got a little disruptive (I've seen actual plays where they came up more often than they didn't), plus I'm not sure I'd say hunger dice have a small effect on the game, not played V5 personally but the anecdotes I've seen are that people find them quite intrusive. <br /> <br /> You might also have missed Curse Dice Tricks; there are some things you can do only with successes on Curse Dice and, if anything, this is a space I'd like to see explored more. <br /> <br /> I'm also not super convinced that it being dangerous to hold too many CDs is or should be a design goal. They're already quite hard to come by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-16T06:02:37-08:00","id":1547777,"title":"","content":"Following up with some additional thoughts:<br /> <br /> I think a big part of the issue here is how Altered Outcomes are framed and how they might or might not be used in the game.<br /> <br /> I do agree that the &quot;only when you're casting a spell or if the GM feels like it&quot; RAW feels anemic and really limits player agency. The list of possible outcomes in the book also feel really decontextualised and generic, probably because they have to be on account of bring a list of general examples. <br /> <br /> But with a little bit of not-even-tweaking-really, just general how-RPGs-work creative engagement, I do think they become quite a powerful tool for making Curse Dice feel important and for making a character's Paths feel impactful. <br /> <br /> Consider the difference between:<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;Okay, that's a Wicked Success&quot; (consults rulebook) &quot;A supernatural being noticed and approves of your actions; so, like, an Angel appears and says well done I guess&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> GM: &quot;Okay, that's a wicked success. What sort of effect do you think that should have?&quot;<br /> Player: &quot;Well I'm a Zed, so my whole thing is bringing endings, and I was trying to shoot the lock off the door, so what if instead of just damaging the lock it rusts away like a couple of centuries have passed?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Or sub in any alternative outcome that fits the character ah the context)<br /> <br /> Similarly I think Curse Dice Tricks should be the sort of things that players are definitely going for consciously, rather than afterthoughts. Like they should be actively trying to extend the range on their actions and get area effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-23T00:23:58-08:00","id":1547904,"title":"","content":"My only comment at this hour of discovery is that, as someone who was a giant fan of Don't Rest Your Head's resolution system between the conflict of getting successes and getting dominance, I feel like curse dice were added specifically to cater to me.<br /> <br /> I'll see if I have more thoughts in the morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-31T13:02:24-08:00","id":1548097,"title":"","content":"The more I look at it, the more I think I'll be switching to &quot;Cursed Energy&quot; and just have it be a supernatural fuel track rather than special dice. You can have special outcomes through dice rolls based on how much &quot;Cursed Energy&quot; a character is holding on to at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}